  "title": "Song dynasty",
  "summary": "The Song dynasty ruled China from 960 to 1279. Founded when Emperor Taizu usurped the Later Zhou throne, it governed as the Northern Song from Bianjing (now Kaifeng) until 1127, when it lost the north to the Jurchen-led Jin, then as the Southern Song, mainly from Lin'an (now Hangzhou), until 1279. It was the first state to issue true paper money, and its era saw commercial growth, printing and civil service examinations.",
